# Fastmail is synced into two local copies:
#
#   ~/Mail/Fastmail  mirror  two-way; what neomutt reads. Deletes and moves
#                            go both ways, so this is NOT an archive.
#   ~/Mail/Vault     vault   pull-only and never deletes: every message that
#                            reached a real folder stays, even after it is
#                            deleted or moved on the server. Browse with
#                            `mail-vault` (read-only).
#
# The app password lives in pass, not in this public repo.

IMAPAccount fastmail
Host imap.fastmail.com
Port 993
TLSType IMAPS
User john@deng.is
PassCmd "pass show Mail/Fastmail/AppPassword"

IMAPStore fastmail-remote
Account fastmail

### Mirror

MaildirStore fastmail-local
Path ~/Mail/Fastmail/
Inbox ~/Mail/Fastmail/INBOX
Flatten .

Channel fastmail
Far :fastmail-remote:
Near :fastmail-local:
Patterns *
Create Both
Remove None
Expunge Both
SyncState *
CopyArrivalDate yes

### Vault

MaildirStore vault-local
Path ~/Mail/Vault/
Inbox ~/Mail/Vault/INBOX
Flatten .

Channel vault
Far :fastmail-remote:
Near :vault-local:
Patterns * !Drafts !Spam !Trash
# Only download new messages: never push, never propagate flags or deletions.
Sync PullNew
Create Near
Remove None
Expunge None
SyncState *
CopyArrivalDate yes
